  "caption_suggestion": "Nominal still-air trajectories for idealised simultaneous burn, series burn without mass release, and two-stage flight with 0 s or 5 s coast after separation. The launch tilt is 1 degree from vertical and the air brake is disabled. Panels (a) and (b) show height and vertical speed; panel (c) shows motor operation, second-motor ignition and separation. Motor-end symbols denote propellant depletion, not the thrust-below-1-lbf sequencing criterion. The staged cases apply a 0.2 s separation delay after the model's low-thrust detector, followed by the stated coast. Events are sampled at 1 ms. The configurations and apogees correspond to Tables 7.1 and 7.2; the unstaged references do not specify a buildable motor installation.",
